{"nodes": [{"id": "prop:composeanimation", "type": "proposition", "title": "prop:composeanimation", "chapter": "Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "group": "ch:Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "level": "medium", "order": 7, "statement": "Let $F\\colon \\sC\\to \\sD$ and $G\\colon \\sD\\to \\sE$ be $1$-sifted-colimit-preserving functors between cocomplete categories generated under colimits by their strongly finitely presented objects.\n\\benum\n\\item \\lab{CA-a}\nThere is a natural transformation from the composite $\\Ani(G)\\circ \\Ani(F)$ to $\\Ani(G\\circ F)$.\n\n\\item \\lab{CA-b}\nIf either $F(\\sC^\\sfp) \\subset \\Ind(\\sD^\\sfp)$ in $\\sD$ or  $(\\Ani(G))(F(\\sC^\\sfp)) \\subset \\sE$ in $\\Ani(\\sE)$, then the natural transformation\n\\[\n\\qq \\Ani(G)\\circ \\Ani(F)\\to \\Ani(G\\circ F)\n\\]\nof \\ref{CA-a} is an equivalence.\n\\eenum", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "0756b9726f5d"}, {"id": "L-underlie", "type": "proposition", "title": "L-underlie", "chapter": "Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "group": "ch:Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "level": "medium", "order": 9, "statement": "In \\uS\\uref{def-setup}, the animated $A$-module that underlies $L_{G_A/A}$ is $e^\\ast(  L_{G/R})\\otimes_R^{\\mathbb L} A$. In particular, the formation of $L_{G_A/A}$ commutes with base change.", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "5792a34f46ed"}, {"id": "thm:padiclimit", "type": "theorem", "title": "thm:padiclimit", "chapter": "Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "group": "ch:Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "level": "medium", "order": 10, "statement": "For a prime $p$, a ring $R$, a commutative, finite, locally free $R$-group $G$ of $p$-power order, and an animated $R$-algebra $A$ such that $\\pi_0(A)$ is $p$-Henselian,\n\\be \n\n\\tst R\\Gamma(A,G)\\isomto R\\lim_n (R\\Gamma(A/^\\bL p^n,G)).\n\\ee", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "6654cee865d8"}, {"id": "thm:strongdescent", "type": "theorem", "title": "thm:strongdescent", "chapter": "Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "group": "ch:Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "level": "medium", "order": 13, "statement": "For a ring $R$ and a commutative, finite, locally free $R$-group $G$, the functor\n\\[\nA\\mapsto R\\Gamma_\\fppf(A,G)\n\\]\nsatisfies fpqc hyperdescent on animated $R$-algebras $A$.", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "eac47e67dc5b"}, {"id": "cor:descentsupport", "type": "corollary", "title": "cor:descentsupport", "chapter": "Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "group": "ch:Flat cohomology with finite, locally free coefficients", "level": "fine", "order": 14, "statement": "Let $R$ be a ring, let $p$ be a prime, let $Z \\subset \\Spec(R/pR)$ be a closed subset, and let $G$ be a commutative, finite, locally free $R$-group of $p$-power order. On animated $R$-algebras $A$, both\n\\[\nA\\mapsto R\\Gamma(A^h_{(p)}, G) \\qxq{and} A\\mapsto R\\Gamma_Z(A,G)\n\\]\nsatisfy hyperdescent for cosimplicial algebras $A \\ra A^\\bullet$ such that $A/^\\bL p \\ra A^\\bullet/^\\bL p$ is an fpqc hypercover.", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "0cb7232b1876"}, {"id": "thm:perfectoidsupport", "type": "theorem", "title": "thm:perfectoidsupport", "chapter": "The characteristic-primary aspects of the main result", "group": "ch:The characteristic-primary aspects of the main result", "level": "medium", "order": 16, "statement": "For a prime $p$, a perfectoid ring $A$, a commutative, finite, locally free, $A$-group $G$ of $p$-power order, and a closed $Z\\subset \\Spec (A/pA)$, we have a functorial in $A$, $G$, and $Z$ identification\n\n\\be \n\nR\\Gamma_Z(A,G)\\cong R\\Gamma_{Z}(\\bA_\\Inf(A), \\bM(G))^{V = 1}.\n\\ee", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "5fa44e423500"}, {"id": "main-pf", "type": "theorem", "title": "main-pf", "chapter": "The characteristic-primary aspects of the main result", "group": "ch:The characteristic-primary aspects of the main result", "level": "medium", "order": 17, "statement": "For a Noetherian local ring $(R,\\mathfrak m)$ that is a complete intersection and a commutative, finite, flat $R$-group $G$,\n\\[\nH^i_{\\mathfrak m}(R,G) \\cong 0 \\qxq{for} i < \\dim(R).\n\\]", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "8ae00d67de4e"}, {"id": "arc-descent", "type": "theorem", "title": "arc-descent", "chapter": "The geometry of integral perfectoid rings", "group": "ch:The geometry of integral perfectoid rings", "level": "medium", "order": 3, "statement": "Let $A$ be a ring \\up{resp.,~with a finitely generated ideal $I \\subset A$} and let $\\sF$ be a torsion sheaf on $A_\\et$. On the category of $A$-algebras $A'$, the functor\n\\[\n\\tst A' \\mapsto R\\Gamma_\\et(A', \\sF)\n\\]\n{\\upshape(}resp.,\n\\[\nA' \\mapsto R\\Gamma_\\et(\\Spec(\\wh{A'})\\setminus V(I), \\sF), \\qx{where the completion is $I$-adic})\n\\]\nsatisfies hyperdescent in the arc \\up{resp.,~$I$-complete arc} topology, and the functor\n\\[\nA' \\mapsto R\\Gamma_\\et(A'^h, \\sF), \\qx{where $(-)^h$ denotes the $I$-Henselization,}\n\\]\nsatisfies hyperdescent in the $I$-complete arc topology.", "uses": [], "sources": ["purity-flat-cohomology"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "0b11bf8ece0d"}], "edges": [], "dangling": [], "meta": {"engine": "hgraph", "entry": "/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/FormalizedPapers/SheavesAndCohomology/PurityFlatCohomology/blueprint/src/content.tex", "macros": {"\\label": "", "\\source": "", "\\dcref": "", "\\uses": "", "\\lean": "", "\\leanok": "", "\\mathlibok": "", "\\notready": "", "\\Spec": "\\operatorname{Spec